;; kotoba/pure route response for a REAL cloud-itonami-app route
;; (cloud.itonami.app.health.v1), served on THIS standalone http-service.mjs
;; demo host -- not a live cloud-itonami-app process.
;;
;; ADR-2608760000 addendum 1: this is the "next slice" that ADR named --
;; porting one already-decision-cored, unauthenticated GET route from
;; cloud-itonami-app onto amu's JVM-free host, as the first pressure test
;; with production logic rather than a synthetic demo.
;;
;; ## What is real vs. representative here
;;
;; The JSON SHAPE (`ok`/`service`/`schema`/`store`/`drive-store` keys) is the
;; real shape `cloud.itonami.app.server/handler`'s `process-liveness?` branch
;; sends (`src/cloud/itonami/app/server.clj`, confirmed 2026-08-29 by curling
;; a live cloud-itonami-app process on 127.0.0.1:1338 and reading server.clj
;; directly). `service` and `schema` are real, fixed constants copied
;; verbatim. `store` and `drive-store` on a REAL server are
;; `(config/store-fingerprint)` and `(name (documents/selected-store-kind))`
;; -- this process's data-directory fingerprint and selected drive backend.
;; THIS host has neither: it is a bare demo process with no data directory
;; and no store. Fabricating a plausible-looking fingerprint here would be
;; exactly the "genuinely fake" health check ADR-2608760000's honesty
;; standard forbids, so both fields say so literally instead of a made-up
;; value.
;;
;; ## What is NOT proven by wiring this route
;;
;; The admission DECISION (is this GET /health) on cloud-itonami-app's real
;; server is `health_core.kotoba`'s `health-route?`, called by
;; `cloud.itonami.app.kotoba-oracle` through the JVM/KIR interpreter. THIS
;; host's admission decision for GET /health is amu's own shared
;; `runtime/http/route-decide.kotoba` (unmodified, table-lookup based) --
;; the same core every other route on this host uses. The two decision cores
;; happen to agree that GET /health is admitted and everything else is not,
;; but this route wiring does not exercise `health_core.kotoba` at all.
;; That comparison is a SEPARATE, more precise claim proven by
;; `scripts/cloud-itonami-health-parity.cljs`: it compiles the same
;; `health_core.kotoba` source (read byte-for-byte from a
;; cloud-itonami-app checkout, unmodified) to this host's `:js-kotoba-v1`
;; target and checks its `health-route?` against the JVM/KIR-interpreter
;; oracle path across a battery of (method, path) inputs.
(ns examples.cloud-itonami-health-route
  (:export [health]))

(defn health
  []
  :string
  (string-concat "{\"ok\":true,\"service\":\"cloud-itonami-app\","
    (string-concat "\"schema\":\"cloud.itonami.app.health.v1\","
      (string-concat "\"store\":\"representative-not-a-live-store-standalone-amu-http-service-demo\","
        "\"drive-store\":\"representative-no-store-on-this-host\"}"))))
